    "pdm_lifestyle_tips_bCbTKb": {
      "type": "pdm_lifestyle-tips",
      "blocks": {
        "tip_WqzmXT": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Exfoliate 1-2 times per week",
            "description": "<p>With an at-home peel that contains Alpha-Hydroxy Acids (AHAs) like glycolic and lactic acids. This will help remove dead skin that has settled into fine lines, making them less visible.</p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/image.jpg",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "tip_qdCXLz": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Reduce sugar intake",
            "description": "<p>Higher blood sugar levels kick-start a process called “glycation,” which makes collagen fibers cross-link, tangling and causing them to lose elasticity. As a consequence, the skin looks wrinkled and saggy. </p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/image_-_2025-01-20T164516.349.png",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "tip_8x8iED": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Sleep on your back to keep your face symmetric and avoid wrinkles",
            "description": "<p>On average, we spend about 2,500 hours a year sleeping. When you sleep on your side, you are squishing your face against the pillow, basically ironing wrinkles into your face. Additionally, gravity acts unevenly, pulling the cheeks and nostrils down. As a result, one side of the face will look slightly rounder (the side on which you sleep) and the other more defined.</p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/image_-_2025-01-20T164637.583.png",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "tip_ChLfdj": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Swap your cotton pillowcase for one containing copper oxide to reduce wrinkles and crow’s feet when you sleep on your side.",
            "description": "<p><strong>Clinical Study</strong>…</p><p>In a 2012 randomized clinical study, participants who slept on a copper pillowcase saw an average 9% reduction in their crow's feet over 8 weeks. Participants not sleeping on the copper cases saw no wrinkle reduction. </p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/image_-_2025-01-20T165310.317.png",
            "sources": "<ul><li>Efficacy of silk-like bedding fabric pillow case in  the treatment of acne vulgaris. (2018). (Link) </li><li>Gadi Borkow, “Using Copper to Improve the Well-Being  of the Skin”, Current Chemical Biology (2014) 8: 89. (Link)</li><li>Mills, O H Jr, and A Kligman. “Acne mechanica.” Archives of dermatology vol. 111,4 (1975): 481-3. (Link)</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "tip_WqzmXT",
        "tip_qdCXLz",
        "tip_8x8iED",
        "tip_ChLfdj"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "section_title": "Skincare is a Lifestyle",
        "section_description": "Caring for your skin goes beyond the products you use. It’s about adopting habits that support your skin’s health every day. Our dermatologists recommend these expert tips to help you reach your skin goals even faster."
      }
    },
